# The launchers for a Mac and Linux keep LF line ends on every checkout, Windows included:
# bash reads a carriage return as part of the command, and a folder moves house by copying.
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.command text eol=lf
# The Windows launchers keep CRLF everywhere: cmd reads a .bat as it runs, line by line, and the
# engine's own checks expect the .bat shape (a push from Windows stores them with LF inside git).
*.bat     text eol=crlf
